      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General procedure for 1–3: LH4 (0.041 g, 0.1 mmol) in methanol (40 mL) was treated with LnCl3·6H2O (0.2 mmol) to give an intense red solution and stirred 20 min at room temperature. H2O3P-tBu (0.014 g, 0.1 mmol) was added, followed by triethylamine (0.04 mL, 0.3 mmol), and the mixture was stirred a further 15 min. Trifluoroacetic acid (0.011 g, 0.1 mmol) was added dropwise with additional triethylamine (0.014 mL, 0.1 mmol) to afford a dark red solution that was stirred overnight at room temperature. The mixture was filtered, the solvent removed in vacuo, and the reddish oily residue washed twice with diethyl ether and dried, then redissolved in methanol and crystallized by slow diffusion of diethyl ether. Block-shaped crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction formed after 9 days. For 1: DyCl3·6H2O (0.075 g, 0.2 mmol); total Et3N 0.054 mL (0.4 mmol).",
